@topic alb_40s
@levels 38-50
@scene barrows_or_avalon
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Explorer
A: barrows or the avalon isle camps for the 40s?
B: stonehenge barrows, everyone knows the pulls and the xp is fast
C: avalon isle, the drakoran camps are open and the view is better
B: the view does not give you levels
C: the empty camp does
A: barrows tonight, avalon on the weekend

@topic scouts
@levels 35-50
@scene scout_range
@role B class=Scout
@role C type=*
A: the other realms say scouts are overpowered at range
B: the other realms have never tried to keep a scout alive up close
C: we do hit hard from very far away though
B: only if they stand in the open. nobody should stand in the open
A: so the advice to the enemy is take cover. noted

# ======================= Hibernia =======================
@realm hib

@topic hib_healer
@levels 20-50
@scene druid_bard_warden
@role B class=Druid
@role C class=Bard
@role D class=Warden
A: druid, bard or warden as the group healer?
B: druid, the heals are biggest and the pet helps in a pinch
C: bard heals and mezzes and gives speed, that is three jobs
D: warden can heal and still take a hit in melee
B: three jobs means none done perfectly
C: none done perfectly beats one done alone
A: two of the three then. bard always

@topic bard
@levels 20-50
@scene bards_do_everything
@role B class=Bard
@role C type=NoLifer
A: why is every hib group built around a bard?
B: speed home, mez on the adds, heals in a pinch. we do it all
C: and you get focused first in every fight because of it
B: which means i am important
C: which means you die first
A: protect the bard, always

@topic enchanter_pbae
@levels 20-50
@scene enchanter_pbae
@role B class=Enchanter
@role C type=Leveler
A: is enchanter area damage too strong in dungeons?
B: pull the room to me and watch it vanish
C: until something resists and the whole room eats you
B: that is what the bard's mez is for
C: and what the druid's rez is for
A: pull carefully then, and stand near the druid

@topic eldritch
